// Four equal bars on a 2:3 field.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Nonbinary pride flag"
  designer "Kye Rowan"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  design-rights "CC-BY-4.0, as the designer states on the flag FAQ"
  date "2014-02"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20230526102227/https://thejasmineelf-blog.tumblr.com/flagfaq"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20180624214236/http://thejasmineelf.tumblr.com/post/77007286542/after-counting-up-all-the-votes-for-each"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20220927074804/https://majesticmess.com/encyclopedia/nonbinary-flag/"
  source "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nonbinary_flag.svg"
  note "Defining sources, both by the designer and read: the designer's flag FAQ, whose hex table gives yellow #FFF433, purple #9B59D0, black #2D2D2D and white, and the final-design post, which gives the meanings. Majestic Mess dates the flag 17 February 2014; Commons and FOTW say February 2014."
  note "The FAQ says the white was originally unmodified white and is now #FFF8E7 (cosmic latte). This file keeps the original, pure white; the later white is a change by the designer and is not written. Her pages state no proportion; 2:3 and equal bars follow the Commons drawing."
  note "This file's license covers the encoding, not the design. The FAQ says the flag is licensed CC BY 4.0 and asks that nobody claim to have designed it."
}
palette {
  yellow "#fff433"
  white "#ffffff"
  purple "#9b59d0"
  black "#2d2d2d"
}
proportion hoist=2 fly=3

bars yellow white purple black
